Article 131 of the Constitution provides Original and Exclusive jurisdiction to the Supreme Court for federal disputes involving questions of legal rights:
1. Between Centre and one or more States;
2. Between Centre and States on one side and other States on the other;
3. Between two or more States.
Inter-state river water disputes (Article 262) and political/commercial disputes are excluded from Article 131.
